  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nSection 6.1 \"the hidden attribute\" states that when scrolling to a hidden=until-found result of find-in-page, the [`beforematch` event should be fired](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-hidden-attribute:~:text=an%20event%20named%20beforematch%20is%20also%20fired%20on%20the%20element).\n\nThere is no information given whether this event should bubble or not (As I understand that means bubbles=false). However, there are [web-platform-tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/0cd9457ec057dd3187792548799d091fc1b9af1d/html/editing/the-hidden-attribute/beforematch-element-fragment-navigation.html#L35-L49) which test for event bubbling.\n\n/cc @emilio @smaug---- @josepharhar ",
